    "created_at": "2020-05-07T20:07:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-05-07T20:07:46Z",
    "body": "The only way I could think of that this would make sense would be if all top layer elements gave `offsetParent` of null, which per @sefeng211's test of fullscreened elements is not true.\r\n\r\nSo our choices are to either update the `offsetParent` spec with a special case for modal dialogs (eww), or call this a Chrome bug. /cc @mfreed7 @chrishtr from Chrome to confirm my reasoning, and to weigh in on which of those two they would prefer.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
