    "updated_at": "2020-05-11T17:19:54Z",
    "body": "Interesting. Well, now it looks like an interop problem with the definition of top layer. Is anyone able to test in Safari? I'm inclined to just go with the majority behavior. I.e. if Safari matches Chrome, then update the offsetParent spec to handle top layer like 2/3 browsers do, and align Firefox to match. Whereas if Safari matches Firefox, then we should consider this a Chrome bug (for both fullscreen and modal dialogs).\r\n\r\n/cc @emilio @zcorpan @tabatkins since this is probably going to end up in CSSWG territory soon, given that it's about https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom-view/#dom-htmlelement-offsetparent",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
